ps":{"d":"M18 20a6 6 0 0 0-12 0"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"10","r":"4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Sign in to sync"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"main","props":{"className":"life-reader life-tip-layout"},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-reader-sidebar life-tip-sidebar"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-back-link","href":"/en/book/05"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},"Back to index"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-sidebar-caption"},"children":["Don’t waste money"]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"aria-label":"Chapter entries"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-01"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["01"]},"Turn off all automatic renewals and switch to manual renewal upon expiry"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["02"]},"Conduct the annual tax reconciliation from March to June; be sure to include all eligible special deductions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-03"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["03"]},"Housing provident fund isn’t just for buying a home: it can be used for renting, home renovations, and paying property taxes, effective from September 20, 2026 under new regulations"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Recalculate your mobile and broadband plans annually: downgrade unused services, and file a complaint if the carrier refuses to comply"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Not buying lottery tickets"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Walk away the moment you see “high returns,” “guaranteed returns,” or “sure profits”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Avoid making minimum payments on credit cards, and never sign up for installment plans or consumer loans for purchases; if borrowing is unavoidable, first convert the interest rate to an annual percentage rate before comparing options"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Don’t give streamers tips, don’t make in‑game purchases, and don’t make impulsive buys"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"When kids make in-app purchases or send gifts, parents can demand refunds for large sums spent by kids over eight if they never gave consent"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Teaching kids one key phrase: anyone who asks them to use a parent’s phone to enter verification codes is a scammer"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Skipping extended warranties for electronics"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Prefer generic drugs that have passed consistency evaluation and those selected in centralized procurement"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Once you set up family medical expense sharing in the yibao app, funds from your individual medical insurance account can be used to pay for your spouse, parents, and children’s medical care and medication"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Drink boiled tap water instead of routinely ordering large water-dispenser bottles or buying small bottled water"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Infrequent stock trading"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Don’t borrow money to invest, avoid leverage, and never buy assets you don’t understand"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Using broad-market index funds instead of actively managed funds as a long-term core holding (the portion of money you keep invested for years)"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"When picking similar funds, go for those with lower fees"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Don’t put all your money into one stock, one platform, or one property"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"Individuals paying income tax at a rate of 10% or higher can open a private pension account; up to 12,000 yuan per year can be deducted from taxable income. For those paying no tax or only a 3% rate, opening such an account is not worthwhile"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-21"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["21"]},"Paying for gym visits individually or on short-term plans is only worthwhile if you have a consistent attendance record spanning over a year"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-22"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["22"]},"Sign a written contract before paying a deposit; if a business faces risks, it must stop taking payments, and you have the right to get back any unused balance if it shuts down"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-23"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["23"]},"Implementing a 24-hour cooling-off period for non-essential big-ticket purchases; making full use of the seven-day no-questions-asked return policy for online shopping"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-24"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["24"]},"Don’t fall for “strikethrough prices” or impulse buying during sales"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-25"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["25"]},"It’s better to choose a non‑return insurance plan and treat any “refunds” or dividends as non‑guaranteed benefits"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-26"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["26"]},"Get sufficient third‑party liability coverage: the mandatory insurance limits are uniform nationwide and relatively low, so any excess must be paid out of your own pocket"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-27"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["27"]},"Set aside an emergency fund equal to 3–6 months of living expenses in a readily accessible account"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-28"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["28"]},"Run a quick comparison before paying off your mortgage — don’t rely on gut feeling"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-29"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["29"]},"When shopping online, follow platform rules and laws — not influencers or “positive reviews”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-30"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["30"]},"If something goes wrong after buying from a livestream, first ask the platform for the seller’s and influencer’s details — they’re required to provide them"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-31"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["31"]},"If you buy unsafe food, you can demand ten times the purchase price as compensation; if the amount is under 1,000 yuan, you’re still entitled to 1,000 yuan"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-32"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["32"]},"Check national inspection reports, 3C certification, and energy labels before buying big-ticket items"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-33"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["33"]},"Bracelets, jade, luxury watches, and collectibles should be judged by “how much you spend” rather than “how much you save”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-34"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["34"]},"For jewelry and gemstones, only test reports bearing the CMA mark are acceptable; you must also verify the issuing agency on the regulator’s official website"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-35"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["35"]},"Random sales such as blind boxes and gacha games are treated as “money that won’t come back”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-36"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["36"]},"If you care about what’s in your food, buy pre-packaged products: loose goods at retail counters aren’t legally required to list ingredients"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-37"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["37"]},"Stocks that have lost value should also be sold according to pre‑set rules — don’t try to even out costs by buying more"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-38"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["38"]},"Planning to invest in overseas assets such as U.S. stocks? Use QDII funds or the Hong Kong Stock Connect program — don’t open accounts with foreign brokers, and don’t use your annual foreign exchange quota for buying foreign stocks"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/05-39","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["39"]},"Only buy insurance for losses your savings can’t cover; use an emergency fund for losses you can afford"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-40"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["40"]},"If someone at home depends on your income, buy term life insurance for the breadwinner first — not for your kids"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-41"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["41"]},"Regretting a personal insurance policy signed for over a year? You can cancel it during the cooling-off period and get most of your premium back"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-42"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["42"]},"Before signing at the bank counter, check whether it’s a deposit or insurance"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-43"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["43"]},"To cancel your insurance policy, contact the insurer directly — don’t use “policy cancellation agents.” If you feel misled, call 12378 for free assistance"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-44"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["44"]},"Writing a specific beneficiary on the policy lets family claim the payout: 5 years for life insurance, 2 years for other policies"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-45"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["45"]},"Do not buy cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin or Tether, or join others’ investment schemes: trades lack legal protection, and suing will not recover investment losses"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/05-46"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["46"]},"If you have no employer, pay into China’s employee pension scheme yourself at the lowest contribution tier and first meet the minimum contribution period; even at the lowest tier, it takes about 10 years of pension payments to recover the cost"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/05"},"children":["Chapter 5"," ·"," ","Don’t waste money"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"05-39"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["39"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-c"},"children":["Evidence"," ","C"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Only buy insurance for losses your savings can’t cover; use an emergency fund for losses you can afford"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["The premiums you pay won’t all be returned to you; a portion goes toward the insurer’s operating costs and profit. Therefore, insurance is worthwhile only for rare events that would otherwise overwhelm your finances — such as serious illness, a car accident causing injury to others, or the death of a primary breadwinner. For smaller losses that your savings can handle, an emergency fund is the better choice."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No money is required. All you need to do is list the major…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Only a fraction of the premiums collected by insurers is paid out as claims. The remainder covers sales, admin…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Only buy insurance for losses your savings can’t cover; use an emergency fund for losses you can afford"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No money is required. All you need to do is list the major potential losses your household might face and determine which ones exceed your savings capacity. This takes about half an hour."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Only a fraction of the premiums collected by insurers is paid out as claims. The remainder covers sales, administration, and profit. Regulations require insurers selling short-term individual health plans to publish their “overall claims ratio” on their website every six months; this figure roughly indicates what proportion of premiums is paid out in claims. On average, buying insurance for any given loss ends up costing you a little extra over time. The upside is that it spreads a potentially catastrophic expense into a series of manageable annual payments. The smaller the loss and the easier it is for you to pay out of pocket, the less advantageous this trade-off becomes. Following this logic, several types of insurance mentioned earlier in this book are worth purchasing: one-year health insurance is covered in Section 7, Item 20; auto liability insurance for drivers is discussed in Item 26 of this section; overseas medical coverage is detailed in Section 21, Item 4; and term life insurance for households dependent on your income is explained in Item 41 of this section (nationwide, effective 2021)."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["中国银保监会办公厅 (2021). 关于规范短期健康保险业务有关问题的通知（银保监办发〔2021〕7 号，综合赔付率按半年在公司官网披露）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2021-01/12/content_5579193.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2021-01/12/content_5579193.htm"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2021-01/12/content_5579193.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["This recommendation is assigned a Grade C because no official statistics exist to determine precisely which policies offer good value. The guidance provided here is meant to help you make a reasoned choice. For low-cost risks — such as cracked phone screens or minor flight delays — you can easily cover the costs yourself, so these policies are generally unnecessary. Similarly, if your savings can sustain you for a year or two without income, you may opt out of critical illness insurance, which compensates for lost earnings during illness. Basic medical insurance is a mandatory social insurance program; it does not fall under this evaluation framework and must be purchased regardless, as explained in Section 7, Item 9. For smaller unexpected expenses, an emergency fund is the appropriate safeguard, as described in Item 27 of this section. Ultimately, the primary beneficiaries of this advice are you and your family."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/05-38"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"chil